d into four legs. The first belongs to the /host\'s/ mother\'s brother, the second to the wife\'s maternal uncle, and the third and fourth are sent to other close relatives. The “leg-bearing relatives on receiving the notification presents the messenger with a strip of red cloth as an expression of gratitude.\'  \'A few days before “Welcoming the Dragon,” messengers must be sent to the family of the wife of the mother\'s brother /chiu-mu; is this an inversion of mu-chiu, “mother\'s brother”?/ to convey the tidings. The host personally goes to engage the services of two Miao sorcerers. The relatives /of the same clan/ in the village are also asked to come to help. For this affair they prepare three kinds of mi-pa, the thunder pa, the dragon pa, and the guest pa, and in addition, a rice dragon must be made.\' '}], {'usage.total_tokens': 990, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 903})
