2026-06-28 09:20:51,403 [INFO] ("During the period from <time-start> to <time-end>, did '<polity>' maintain a courier system, defined as a government-operated postal service for relaying messages and orders—where couriers (čāpārs) used riding animals obtained from locals, sometimes requisitioned, and the service was also used by spies to transmit intelligence—even though a formal system of relay stations no longer existed? Strictly choose an option from the unordered set {A, B}. A = present, B = absent", None, [{'role': 'system', 'content': "You are are history professor writing challenging questions for PhD students.\n\n    Your task is to create a challenging yet well-defined historical exam question based on a variable definition from a historical dataset.\n    Follow the rules below, and return ONLY the final question template, based on the examples provided. \n    \n    1. Begin the question with a concise explanation of the variable's definition, strictly adhering to the provided description, if no description is provided, use the variable name as the basis for the question.\n    2. Ensure all of the following template markers are used:\n        - '<polity>' for polity names (e.g. 'The Papal States')\n        - '<time-start>' and '<time-end>' for temporal scope\n    3. The question should make abundantly clear what the format of the desired response is and that only that response should be given.\n    4. The output must be exactly one question, and must end with a question mark (?).\n\n    Structure your response with a clear question template.\n    "}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Variable name: atlatl\n"Variable description: The absence or presence of atlatl as a military technology used in warfare.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "Consider the period from <time-start> to <time-end> in the context of '<polity>'. Was the atlatl, defined as a spear-throwing device used to increase the range and force of a projectile, absent or present as a 'military techno